  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_019, a multimodal multiprofile model using PCA, ResNet, avgpool, and weighted fusion with validation accuracy 0.639 and F1 0.620. The main unresolved uncertainty is RNA representation, since only PCA has been tested, while the current best fusion, aggregation, profile, and image settings are already relatively well supported. config_031 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 while keeping the known-good multimodal multiprofile, avgpool, weighted-fusion, and ResNet configuration. This will clarify whether a learned RNA encoder can improve the best current direction or whether PCA is already sufficient. It is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest known configuration while testing a major representation decision in a single-factor comparison."
